RHCSA Day 5 (Rewrite) — Kernel, Boot Process & GRUB on Rocky Linux VM

This is an in-depth rewrite of Day 5 focusing entirely on the kernel, boot process, GRUB bootloader, systemd targets, and kernel modules — the areas where confidence matters most on exam day. We'll use a Rocky Linux 9 VM (via VirtualBox/KVM) for safe, repeatable practice.

⚠️ Why not Podman? Containers share the host kernel and have no real bootloader, GRUB, or initramfs. You cannot practice boot interruption, GRUB editing, rd.break, or systemd target switching inside a container. Use a full VM (VirtualBox, KVM/libvirt, or GNOME Boxes) with snapshots so you can break things and roll back instantly.
